post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

One command finishes the setup - it helps you choose a speech model and tells you
how to get it, starts the server, and reads your keys off the keyboard so no
keycode is ever typed by hand:

  talkey-setup

It installs nothing on your behalf. Safe to re-run, and `talkey-setup keys`
rebinds whenever you like.

If anything is ever wrong, one command tells you what and how to fix it:

  talkey doctor

Note talkey types with xdotool, which is X11 only - on Wayland nothing arrives
in your window. `talkey doctor` says so plainly.

Rather do it by hand? Every step is in /usr/share/doc/talkey-git/README.md.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Note: ~/.config/i3/talkey.conf is your copy - this upgrade did not touch it.
Compare it against /usr/share/talkey/bindings/i3.conf if bindings changed, or
re-run `talkey-setup keys` to regenerate it.
EOF
}
